==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Red EnerG]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 80~83.33 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,500f</sup>.
*4 [[Red EnerG]]s spawn after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Red EnerG]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Assassin Bear]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 80~83.33 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,500f</sup>.
*3 [[Red EnerG]]s spawn after 96.67 seconds<sup>2,900f</sup>, delay 36.67~43.33 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Red EnerG]]s spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Because Red EnerGs are spammed in this stage, you will inevitably face off an endless stream of surge attacks. It definitely doesn't help that each have nearly 700k health. [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]] and his Immune to Surge Talent works wonders here as its recharge time is just enough to mirror that of the Red EnerGs, allowing it to perfectly stall them, [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] is also great here, due to his health at level 43 allows it to tank 3 hits from the Red EnerGs on 1 crown and 4 crowns, and 2 hits for 2-3 crowns, allowing an easier start off. You will need either Stone Cat or the normal Cat Cannon to kill the Assassin Bears. Beyond them, you'll need a lot of good Surge Immune attackers, and chances are you might not have the necessary units or resources for the stage.

Spawn Gato Amigo at about a 3 second rate (Red EnerG's attack rate is 2.97 seconds), and use [[Cat Cannon|Breakerblast]] to sync up the Red EnerGs. Then you can use whatever surge immune unit you want, such as talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]]. Once the Red EnerGs are synced, you can summon [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to deal big damage to the multiple EnerGs at one go, ideally knocking them back.

==Trivia==
*The Japanese name of this stage, Issunsaki wa Sumi ("Ahead Lies Charcoal" or lit. "Charcoal is One Step Ahead"), is a play on the phrase "issunsaki wa yami," which means, "the future could hold anything," but literally translates to "darkness is one step ahead."
*Going along with the theme of meat and cooking in [[Rose-Colored Road]], Ashes Just Ahead's Japanese name refers to charcoal, which has a wide range of applications in cooking.

